   plain='The Centre holds the richer taxes; the States hold more of the duties. Money flows to the States by two routes: Finance Commission devolution and grants (a rule-based, untied right) and scheme-based transfers (the Centre’s choice, often with conditions). The more devolution, the less is left for tied schemes. The handout traces the shift from the Planning Commission’s command and control to NITI Aayog’s cooperative federalism.',
